            <ArticleTitle>Cryptorchism with a large abdominal mass--a challenge.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>946-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The undescended testis is associated with an increased incidence of testicular malignancy. The position of the undescended testis is related to the likelihood of carcinogenesis, with the intra-abdominal testis having the highest malignant potential. We present 3 patients to illustrate this tendency and to highlight the unusual presentation as an &quot;acute abdomen&quot;.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
